hey hey let's go on a real hunt it's  been a while since we've gotten a new  Assassin's Creed game and Ubisoft  promises origins to be a fresh take on  the franchise while origin still has  some things you'd expect from an AC game  here are some of the biggest changes  while you will still be assassinating  countless people Assassin's Creed origin  serves as a good jumping on point for  new players it takes place in Egypt well  before the first game and features a  fresh new cast of characters you play as  by Ekta last Magi as Cleopatra is  overthrowing your brother and ascending  the throne while you'll find references  to previous games new players should  have no trouble following the story this  time around say goodbye to the mini-map  and hello to the compass on the top of  your screen you'll find a Skyrim like  compass that's populated with question  marks and other points of interest this  may seem like a small change but it  feeds into a stronger sense of  exploration rather than constantly  pulling up your map or checking the  mini-map to reach your destination  just follow the objective marker on the  compass now you can admire the beautiful  views of Egypt and follow your intuition  in the seamless world  [Music]  the combat in Origins has gone through  an overhaul the free-flowing combat of  previous games has been replaced with a  Dark Souls esque hitbox style detection  combat this means you'll need to read  your opponent's time your dodges and get  behind your enemies to deliver powerful  blows while you could use different  weapons in previous Assassin's Creed  games origins boasts a wide range of  different weapon types that all play and  feel different axes are slower but pack  a punch while dual swords force byuk to  get in close with speedy hacks and  slashes origins plays more like an  action RPG than its predecessors this  means that as you kill enemies complete  quests and find new locations you will  gain experience and level up weapons  will have a level requirement and quest  in regions will have a suggested level  although nothing is really stopping you  from checking out a high level area or  tackling a quest that might be a little  too hard for byuk loot goes hand in hand  with most RPGs and origins is no  different there are three tiers of  rarity regular rare and legendary or  blue purple and yellow for the most part  you get weapons randomly but certain  quests will net you legendary weapons  with special perks pretty much  everything you equip will have a rarity  tier however costumes do not affect your  stats no matter the rarity thanks for  watching and if you want to know we  thought of assassin's creed origins be  sure to check out our review on GameSpot  calm  [Applause]  why is this gladiator running in circles  you
 

